# Local Worker Health ([PROJECT_NAME])

Read when:

1. configuring the local worker lane,
2. validating worker readiness,
3. troubleshooting degraded or offline worker behavior,
4. deciding whether worker packets are safe to issue.

Skip when:

1. the project is cloud-only or local-worker delegation is disabled.

## Purpose

This file proves the local worker is healthy enough for bounded implementation work.

It records:

1. how the worker is reached,
2. what health checks have passed,
3. what secret and network boundary applies,
4. what degraded or offline rules apply.

## Current Worker Route

- Local worker enabled: YES / NO / PLANNED
- Worker tool or client:
- Endpoint type: OpenAI-compatible / native extension / local CLI / other
- Endpoint URL or command:
- Primary coding model:
- Tool-calling support required: YES / NO
- Last health check:
- Health status: OK / DEGRADED / OFFLINE / UNKNOWN

Do not store secrets here.
Store private keys, tokens, and sensitive host details in private operator configuration.

## Minimum Health Checks

Before worker implementation packets are allowed:

- [ ] Worker endpoint or command is reachable from the development machine.
- [ ] Expected model is visible or selectable.
- [ ] Worker can read one allowed file and summarize it accurately.
- [ ] Worker can perform one sandbox or doc-only edit successfully.
- [ ] Worker can run the allowed command set or clearly report command limitations.
- [ ] Worker returns structured result packets instead of broad prose.
- [ ] Timeout behavior is known and recorded in packet or session-state artifacts.

## Sandbox And Secret Boundary

- Worker execution location: same checkout / dedicated worktree / disposable checkout / remote sandbox
- Secrets available to worker: NO / YES + rationale
- Network access during worker loop: NONE / LAN / INTERNET + rationale
- Push or deploy allowed from worker: NO unless explicitly packet-authorized
- Tier C ready: YES / NO / N/A

For Tier C or sensitive-data work, worker implementation packets are blocked until secrets are unavailable by default and rollback or snapshot commands are recorded in the packet.

## Optional Endpoint Smoke Command

If the worker exposes an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, record a project-specific smoke command such as:

```bash
python3 scripts/check_openai_compatible_endpoint.py \
  --base-url http://<local-worker-host>:<port>/v1 \
  --api-key test-key \
  --expect-model <model-or-alias>
```

If no endpoint exists, replace this with the exact local CLI or extension smoke path.

## Degraded Or Offline Rules

- Attended session: one bounded cloud-only fallback slice is allowed only when already surfaced to the operator.
- Unattended session: halt instead of silently falling back to cloud-only work.
- Infrastructure outage is not investigator work.
- Two malformed or timed-out results after the worker is otherwise healthy means worker setup needs tuning before more packets.

